  "goodToKnow": "Der Winterschlaf is hibernation: Igel, Murmeltiere and Fledermäuse halten Winterschlaf. Bears in fact have a lighter Winterruhe (winter rest). Der Siebenschläfer (edible dormouse) sleeps for about seven months. The Siebenschläfertag on 27 June is named after a legend of seven sleeping saints, not the animal; weather lore says the weather then lasts seven weeks. Figuratively, aus dem Winterschlaf erwachen means to wake from inactivity. It has no plural."
